{"result":"{
  "id": "18362",
  "key": "SFCC-196",
  "summary": "PDP UI – Maximum Purchase Quantity",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper,\n\n**I want** to be clearly informed when I've reached the maximum purchase limit for a product,\n\n**so that** I understand why I can't add more to my bag.\n\n----\n\nScreenshot (Figma is leading): \n\n![\"image-20260729-014706.png\"](image-20260729-014706.png)\n\nSFCC enforces a configurable maximum purchase quantity at a global level. Initially, this will be set at 3. Since the PDP has no quantity selector, enforcement is triggered when a shopper clicks Add to Bag multiple times for the same size. The system tracks how many units of the same variant are already in the shopper's bag and prevents addition beyond the configured limit. When the limit is reached, an inline message is displayed.",
  "status": {
    "name": "Ready for SIT",
    "category": "Done",
    "color": "green"
  },
  "labels": [
    "Custom",
    "DesignDependent",
    "PRD-011",
    "Squad-A"
  ],
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "# Given a shopper clicks Add to Bag and the configured maximum purchase quantity(for now set at 3) has not yet been reached, when the action is confirmed, then the item is added to bag successfully.\n# Given a shopper clicks Add to Bag and the configured maximum purchase quantity (for now set at 3) has been reached (counting size variant units already in bag), when the action is attempted, then the item is not added, the “Add to Bag” CTA is disabled, and an inline message is displayed informing the shopper of the limit.\n# Given a shopper clicks Add to Bag for size B for the same product (and if applicable, same colour) after reaching the configured maximum purchase limit for size A (for now set at 3), then the item is added to bag successfully.\n# Given there is no maximum purchase quantity configured (please note: this is unlikely to happen in production, but we can test the behaviour if it’s set to blank), when the shopper clicks Add to Bag, then no restriction is applied and standard Add to Bag behaviour applies."
  }
}"}

