{"result":"{
  "id": "18523",
  "key": "SFCC-268",
  "summary": "PDP – Maximum Purchase Quantity – BM Config",
  "description": "**As a** Site Admin, \n\n**I want** to configure a global default maximum purchase quantity in Business Manager, \n\n**so that** a purchase limit is enforced across all products and all shoppers without requiring a code deployment.\n\n----\n\nThis story covers the global default configuration only. It acts as the fallback when no SKU-level or customer group-level override is set (covered in SFCC-703). Enforcement and messaging on the PDP are covered in SFCC-196.",
  "status": {
    "name": "Ready for SIT",
    "category": "Done",
    "color": "green"
  },
  "labels": [
    "CAI-017",
    "Custom",
    "PRD-011",
    "Squad-A"
  ],
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "1. Given I am a Site Admin in Business Manager, when I navigate to the relevant configuration, then I can view and edit a global default maximum purchase quantity.\n2. Given the global default is set, when a shopper adds a product to bag, then that value is used as the purchase limit on a size variant level.\n3. Given I update the global default, when I save, then the change takes effect without a code deployment.\n4. Given the global default is blank, when the system resolves the limit, then no purchase restriction is applied, and standard Add to Bag behaviour applies."
  }
}"}

